  task("dudect:canary", "Validate dudect harness: leaky early-exit must trip, honest ct_eq_bytes must not") do ->
    # NET.4.2 verification (canary half). Pure-Quartz port of dudect
    # (Reparaz/Balasch/Verbauwhede 2017) — Welch's t-test over timing
    # samples, 102 parallel tests (1 uncropped + 100 exponentially-cropped
    # + 1 second-order). The canary spec exercises both directions: a
    # deliberately-leaky early-exit ct_eq_bytes that MUST trip the harness
    # (|t| >= 100 — "overwhelming evidence" per Reparaz §4), and the
    # honest subtle::ct_eq_bytes that must NOT trip (|t| < 5). Validates
    # the harness's discrimination before any real-primitive test relies
    # on it. Same compile/link/run pipeline as ed25519:smoke.
    var compiler = compiler_path()
    if exists(compiler) == 0
      fail("Compiler not found at #{compiler} — run 'quake build' first")
    end
    if sh_maybe("command -v clang > /dev/null 2>&1") != 0
